    "entry": 547820,
    "text": "The routine adds a number display control to a scripted window, with the same steps and record layout as the number entry routine at `0x085A5C`. r3 is the address of the result word and r4 points to the record (`0x085BF4`, `0x085BF8`). Word +0 gives the window through the lookup at `0x0848D8` and a dynamic_cast with flag 0 (`0x085C04` to `0x085C1C`). A null cast result copies the word at data+0x77374, the none value (an inference), to the result word and ends (`0x085C28`, `0x085D18` to `0x085D20`). The routine saves the old port at 60(1) and makes the window's port current (`0x085C2C` to `0x085C40`).\n\nWords +4 and +8 become the position shorts at 58(1) and 56(1), and words +12 and +16 become the width and the height (`0x085C48` to `0x085CA0`). Virtual slot 236 receives the addresses of the position shorts (`0x085C88` to `0x085CA4`).\n\nThe TWNumber constructor receives the window, the position, the width and the height (`0x085CC0` to `0x085CD8`). The routine then adds the widget to the window (`AddWidget`) (`0x085CE0` to `0x085CEC`). The routine registers the widget with the number 18 (`0x085CF4` to `0x085D04`) and restores the port (`0x085D08`, `0x085D0C`). A null from operator new skips the constructor (`0x085CBC`) but not the later calls."
